@@ -58,6 +58,12 @@ No `patches.py`. `op_mode` stays docked: Odyssey only takes its motion moves in
 
 General host and tool changes first needed here; each applies to every game:
 
+- **Opt-in cold vertex/pixel loading:** [Joined loading for a demanded cold pair](../../../docs/reference/shaders.md#opt-in-joined-loading-for-a-demanded-cold-vertex-and-pixel-pair). Default off; native fixture checks do not establish a device performance gain.
+
+- **Disjoint long-frame creation timing:** [Nested prediction libraries counted twice in long-frame totals](../../../docs/reference/frame-rate.md#nested-prediction-libraries-counted-twice-in-long-frame-totals). Measurement correction only; device performance is not implied.
+
+- **CRLF prewarm parsing (source audit; device validation pending):** [CRLF prewarm rows retain a carriage return](../../../docs/reference/shaders.md#crlf-prewarm-rows-retain-a-carriage-return). The observed iPad list was LF; this hardening preserves its cache format and does not explain the recorded first-use hitches.
+
 - **BAHS pairs omitted from vertex padding:** [Pixel shader inputs the vertex shader does not write](../../../docs/reference/shaders.md#pixel-shader-inputs-the-vertex-shader-does-not-write).
 - **Front end at `-O1`** (`dmsh_build.py` and `ios_metal.py`): [Front end at -O1: Apple's control-flow lowering](../../../docs/reference/shaders.md#front-end-at--o1-apples-control-flow-lowering).
 - **Pipeline archive flush periods** (no compile waits for a flush; the prepare step stops at the last pair handed out): [A compile that does not return stalls every flush and draw](../../../docs/reference/shaders.md#a-compile-that-does-not-return-stalls-every-flush-and-draw).
