+### CRLF prewarm rows retain a carriage return
+
+- **Symptom:** a Windows-authored pair list gives a pixel key ending in a carriage return, or equivalent LF and CRLF learned pipeline rows are not deduplicated.
+- **Cause:** splitting only at LF leaves one trailing CR in the last field and in the text deduplication key. Shader-map keys and newly recorded pipeline rows have no such terminator.
+- **Fix:** `nvn_line_without_cr` removes exactly one final CR before pair parsing, warm-list parsing and user-row deduplication. Spaces, the binary render-key format, existing files and cache markers remain unchanged. This is separate from the shell input-stamp trim in the F1 host.
