 - **Symptom:** the ground kept stale 32×32 blocks where the G-buffer draw failed the depth test: blocks of a stale image where a depth pre-pass and a later pass with other vertex shaders meet (Odyssey: 32×32 blocks on every fourth frame).
@@ -964,3 +972,12 @@ Finding, keying and translating shaders (`dm/gfx/tools/shader_split.py`, `dmsh_b
 - **Fix:** `dmsh_geometry.capture` initializes only words absent from the captured outputs. The capture slot map stores each selected word once, including defaults for absent outputs. Position W, point size, generic W, clip distances, layer and viewport retain their existing bit values. Full capture selects all 144 words; lean capture selects its consumed words. Shaders and host must be rebuilt together.
 - **Check:** the synthetic throughput comparison alternates control/candidate order and verifies all 9,437,184 captured words against both the original buffer and literal expected values. Mac runs vary in timing, so their percentage gain does not establish iPhone gameplay FPS. The optional real-translator capture fixture in `t_geometry` also checks all uncaptured defaults. All 1,225 NieR shaders build for Mac and iPhone; standard geometry replay and dependency checks pass.
 - **Found on:** [NieR:Automata US 1.0.3](../../dm/games/010056B015FE8000/README.md#factory-combat-capture-and-9s-texture-follow-up), iPhone City Ruins: 14 geometry groups in the captured frame spend 7.485 ms in vertex capture, 6.512 ms in compute and 1.019 ms in depth raster. The accompanying pass dump affects total frame time; its large uncovered GPU interval must not be treated as a clean gameplay hitch measurement.
+
+
+### Opt-in joined loading for a demanded cold vertex and pixel pair
+
+- **Symptom:** the first resolution of a normal two-stage program loads its missing vertex and pixel libraries serially on the submit thread.
+- **Cause:** `prog_get` ordinarily calls `shader_get` for each stage in order. These are both required by the same program, unlike speculative future prefetch.
+- **Experiment:** `DM_NVN_PAIR_LOAD=1` joins two parallel `shader_load` calls only when the program has exactly one mapped vertex and one pixel stage, distinct keys, both absent from the cache, and prewarm has started, finished and left no pending items. The default remains the original path. Workers return attempt-local objects; the submit thread publishes and records successful stages in original order. Failures are not immediately retried by the same program lookup and are not entered into a new global failure cache. Geometry, compute, builtins, layer variants, cached stages and single-miss cases keep their original path.
+- **Check:** `test_nvn_pair_batch.py` plus the native Foundation fake-loader fixture check gates, joined execution, local failure results and ARC ownership without a GPU. The period summary reports batch/count/time only when enabled. Parallel construction may increase temporary memory or compiler contention; a device A/B with nonzero eligible batches is required before enabling it by default or claiming a speedup. Existing shader options and cache identities do not change.
+- **Found on:** the [Odyssey iPad first-use audit](../../dm/games/0100000000010000/README.md#found-on-this-game). This is a controlled experiment, not a device-validated FPS improvement.
